{:fh/id  "FH-CTRL-015"
 :fh/law "An INVALID submit is attemptable and it REVEALS: attempting marks the form attempted, which shows every error at once including on leaves the user never visited, and attempting again after a failure is an ordinary thing a user does rather than a state the form refuses. A VALID submit additionally opens a pending save stamped with its attempt number, and that stamp is the staleness fence — a reply carrying a superseded number is INERT, while the three shapes a reply takes (rebase, set-errors, reset) each settle the pending submit exactly once."

 :baseline {:title "" :body "words"}

 :title-path [:title]
 :body-path  [:body]

 :errors {[:title] "required"}

 ;; BEFORE any attempt: the error exists and is not revealed, because the
 ;; user has not been to that leaf.
 :show-error-before? false

 ;; THE INVALID ATTEMPT. Attempted, revealed, and no save opened.
 :attempted-after-invalid?   true
 :attempts-after-invalid     1
 :pending-after-invalid      nil
 :show-error-after-invalid?  true

 ;; A SECOND invalid attempt is accepted — the counter moves and the form
 ;; is not wedged.
 :attempts-after-second-invalid 2
 :pending-after-second-invalid  nil

 ;; THE VALID ATTEMPT, once the errors are cleared. The pending token is
 ;; the attempt number, so it is monotone and comparable.
 :attempts-after-valid 3
 :pending-after-valid  3

 ;; THE STALE REPLY. A reply from attempt 3 arrives after the user has
 ;; submitted a fourth time; its token is not the pending one, so it is
 ;; inert.
 :stale-token       3
 :attempts-after-fourth 4
 :pending-after-fourth  4
 :stale-reply-current?  false
 :fresh-reply-current?  true

 ;; THE THREE SHAPES A REPLY TAKES, each settling the pending submit.
 :saved-values     {:title "Ready" :body "words"}
 :pending-after-rebase     nil
 :server-errors    {[:title] "taken"}
 :pending-after-set-errors nil
 :pending-after-reset      nil

 ;; And the reveal survives a reply: an error that arrived from the server
 ;; after a submit is shown, because the form is still attempted.
 :show-server-error? true}
